---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Solution C: Service Area Pages Drive Growth"
  description="Case Study: How service area pages multiplied organic impressions by 214% and inbound leads by 138% in 4 months."
>
  <section class="py-20 lg:py-24 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <div class="mb-12">
        <span class="bg-brand-blue/20 text-brand-blue text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-widest px-6 py-2 rounded-full border border-brand-blue/30 shadow-[0_0_15px_rgba(30,144,255,0.2)]">Solution C</span>
        <h1 class="font-heading text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-6 leading-tight">
          Service Area Pages That<br/>
          <span class="bg-clip-text text-transparent bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-cyan via-brand-blue to-brand-sky">
            Multiplied Organic Reach
          </span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-brand-sky/80 leading-relaxed">
          A local agency was ranking well in its home town but invisible everywhere else. By adding city-specific service area pages, we multiplied its organic reach and turned nearby search traffic into real leads.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none">
        <div class="bg-brand-darkest border border-brand-blue/20 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-white font-heading text-2xl mb-4">The Challenge</h2>
          <p class="text-white/80">
            This agency ran a single homepage that talked about its services without ever naming the places it served. Google had no way to connect the business to the communities around it. The result: it dominated searches in its own city — its flagship "home territory" keyword ranked in the top 3 — but earned almost zero visibility in the surrounding towns where it also worked. Nearly all of its strongest keywords were stuck outside the local "map pack," and qualified nearby customers simply never found it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-white font-heading text-2xl mb-4">The Solution</h2>
        <p class="text-white/80 mb-6">
          We built a dedicated, keyword-mapped service area page for every community the agency actually serves. Instead of a thin "areas we serve" list, each page was treated as a real ranking asset—with unique local copy, on-page optimization, and clean URL structure.
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-4 text-white/80 mb-12">
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="text-brand-cyan">✦</span>
            <span><strong>City-Specific Pages:</strong> One page per served city, mapped to its own keywords (e.g. "flooring contractor in Hendersonville") rather than competing for the same home-town terms.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="text-brand-cyan">✦</span>
            <span><strong>Unique Local Content:</strong> Every page included genuinely distinct copy referencing local landmarks, neighborhoods, and community context—no duplicated boilerplate that would trigger thin-content penalties.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="text-brand-cyan">✦</span>
            <span><strong>On-Page & Technical SEO:</strong> Unique title tags, meta descriptions, H1/H2 targeting, internal linking from the homepage and service pages, and proper schema markup for each location.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="text-brand-cyan">✦</span>
            <span><strong>Interlinked Service Hub:</strong> Each service area page linked to relevant services and back, spreading authority across the whole site instead of funneling everything into one page.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="text-brand-cyan">✦</span>
            <span><strong>Local SEO Alignment:</strong> We aligned the new pages with Google Business Profile data and local citations so search engines connected the dots for each geography.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <div class="bg-brand-darkest border border-brand-blue/20 rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-white font-heading text-2xl mb-4">The Results — In Just 4 Months</h2>
          <p class="text-white/80 mb-8">
            The service area pages didn't just rank—they began capturing traffic for an entirely new set of high-intent, local-search keywords the site had never been visible for before.
          </p>
          <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6 text-center">
            <div>
              <p class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-cyan mb-2">+214%</p>
              <p class="text-white/60 text-sm italic">Organic Impressions</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-cyan mb-2">+138%</p>
              <p class="text-white/60 text-sm italic">Inbound Leads</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-cyan mb-2">Top 3</p>
              <p class="text-white/60 text-sm italic">For New Local Keywords</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-white font-heading text-2xl mt-12 mb-4">Why This Works</h2>
        <p class="text-white/80">
          Google rewards relevance and specificity. A single homepage can only credibly target one "home" geography. By giving each city its own dedicated page, we gave search engines a clean, authoritative answer for every local query the agency wanted to win—turning invisible nearby markets into its biggest new source of leads.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-12 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6 justify-center">
          <a 
            href="/services/case-studies/solution-b/"
            class="inline-block border border-brand-blue/50 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-lg font-bold hover:bg-brand-blue/10 transition-all duration-300"
          >
            ← View Solution B
          </a>
          <a 
            href="/contact/"
            class="cta-glow-shine inline-block bg-brand-accent text-[#0A0A0A] px-10 py-4 rounded-xl font-bold hover:bg-brand-accent-light"
          >
            Grow Your Local Reach
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-center text-brand-sky/60 text-sm mt-6">
          See the full story from <a href="/services/case-studies/solution-a/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Solution A</a> to <a href="/services/case-studies/solution-b/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Solution B</a>, or view <a href="/services/case-studies/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">all case studies</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>